cooler, winter-escape)","shoulder":"May-Jun + Nov (warm, softer rates, windy - windsurf shoulder)","green":"Sep-Oct (warmest, quietest, best value; south of the belt)","booking_lead":"Palm/Eagle resorts + AI 2-5 mo (peak Dec-Apr + Hi-Winds); dives/windsurf/Arikok 1-2 wk","off_season_specials":"Sep-Oct value beach weeks; windsurf/kite packages (windiest May-Jul); Arikok + flamingo + lighthouse add-ons","event_peaks":"Aruba Hi-Winds (Jun/Jul, Caribbean''s biggest windsurf event); Carnival (Jan-Feb); Dec-Apr high season; Soul Beach (verify)","campaign_start":"Dec-Apr beach weeks by Aug (winter-escape); warm-value Sep-Oct by Jul; Hi-Winds windsurf by Apr; Carnival ~3 mo ahead"},"jewels":[{"name":"Eagle Beach","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"via hotel/day","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"si":"tropical","when":"year-round","commission":"bed-bank/hotel affiliate"},{"name":"The Palm Beach resort strip","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$250-900+/night","timing":"year-round; Dec-Apr peak","draw_rank":2,"hook":"the high-rise heart — watersports, casinos, dining and nightlife on a calm swimming beach, the easy all-in-one base","si":"tropical","blurb":"the high-rise heart — watersports, casinos, dining and nightlife on a calm swimming beach, the easy all-in-one base","when":"year-round; Dec-Apr peak","commission":"consortia/host + bed-bank"},{"name":"The SS Antilla ''Ghost Ship'' wreck","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$50-120/pp","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-op/OTA 8-12%"},{"name":"Hadicurari (Fisherman''s Huts) windsurf + Hi-Winds","si_tag":"ocean","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$40-160/pp","timing":"year-round; windiest May-Jul","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the Caribbean''s windsurf/kite mecca of steady trades — beginner lessons to pro flatwater-and-wave, and the region''s biggest windsurf tournament each June/July","si":"ocean","blurb":"the Caribbean''s windsurf/kite mecca of steady trades — beginner lessons to pro flatwater-and-wave, and the region''s biggest windsurf tournament each June/July","when":"year-round; windiest May-Jul","commission":"operator/affiliate 10-15%"},{"name":"Renaissance Island + a resort honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$300-900+/night","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a private-island flamingo beach, sunset sails and Palm/Eagle resort romance — an easy, sure-weather Caribbean honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"a private-island flamingo beach, sunset sails and Palm/Eagle resort romance — an easy, sure-weather Caribbean honeymoon","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"resort/consortia"},{"name":"Arikok National Park + the Natural Pool","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$40-160/pp + park fee","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~20% of the island — cacti, lava, limestone cliffs, coves, and the volcanic-rock Natural Pool","si":"adventure","blurb":"~20% of the island — cacti, lava, limestone cliffs, coves, and the volcanic-rock Natural Pool","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"operator/affiliate"},{"name":"The flamingos of Renaissance Island","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","price_band":"day-pass ~$100-150","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"hook":"wade with Aruba''s famous pink flamingos on a private-island beach — one of the Caribbean''s signature wildlife photo-ops","si":"adventure","blurb":"wade with Aruba''s famous pink flamingos on a private-island beach — one of the Caribbean''s signature wildlife photo-ops","when":"year-round","commission":"resort/affiliate"},{"name":"Palm Beach casinos + Oranjestad","si_tag":"nightlife","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-120/pp","timing":"year-round, evenings","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the resort strip''s casinos, bars and live music, plus the pastel-Dutch capital of Oranjestad — the region''s easy evening scene","si":"nightlife","blurb":"the resort strip''s casinos, bars and live music, plus the pastel-Dutch capital of Oranjestad — the region''s easy evening scene","when":"year-round, evenings","commission":"venue/bundle"},{"name":"The Aruban table","si_tag":"culinary","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-150/pp","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"keshi yena, fresh fish and food-truck culture, plus a strong Palm Beach/Oranjestad restaurant scene — a Dutch-Caribbean plate with range","si":"culinary","blurb":"keshi yena, fresh fish and food-truck culture, plus a strong Palm Beach/Oranjestad restaurant scene — a Dutch-Caribbean plate with range","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"venue/bundle"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Aruba?","a":"Not storms or crime - small stuff. Aruba is south of the hurricane belt (very low storm risk) and low-crime, so plan for petty theft, strong sun and dengue, plus no-fly 18-24h if you dive the Antilla. It''s about as low-stress as Caribbean travel gets.","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to go to Aruba?","a":"Year-round - Aruba is warm, dry and reliably sunny with no real storm season. December-April is peak (winter escape, highest prices); May-August is warm, quieter value and windiest (best for windsurf and Hi-Winds).","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which beach - Eagle or Palm?","a":"Both: Eagle Beach for the wide, quiet, top-rated sand and fofoti trees; Palm Beach for the resort strip, watersports and nightlife. Most people beach at Eagle and stay at Palm.","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Do I need to be a diver to see the Antilla wreck?","a":"No - the water is so clear that snorkelers can see the 400-ft wreck from the surface in ~60ft, and most excursions include boat, snorkel gear and guiding. Certified divers penetrate deeper sections (advanced); everyone else snorkels the shallows (no no-fly restriction).","source":"visitaruba.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Aruba good for windsurfing or a wildlife day?","a":"Both are signatures. Hadicurari (Fisherman''s Huts) is a world-class windsurf/kite beach (Hi-Winds each June/July), and you can wade with flamingos on Renaissance Island or hike Arikok National Park to the Natural Pool - beyond the beach, Aruba has real range.","source":"aruba.com","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Aruba Travel Guide: Eagle & Palm Beach, the Antilla Wreck, Arikok & Windsurfing","meta_description":"Plan Aruba - the Caribbean''s sure-thing sun, safely south of the hurricane belt: top-rated Eagle Beach, the 400-ft Antilla wreck (snorkelable), world-class Hadicurari windsurfing, Arikok National Park and the Natural Pool, and the flamingos of Renaissance Island.","slug":"aruba","primary_keyword":"Aruba travel guide","long_tail":["Eagle Beach Aruba","Antilla wreck dive snorkel","Aruba Hi-Winds windsurfing Hadicurari","Arikok National Park Natural Pool","Renaissance Island flamingos","is Aruba safe"],"search_language":"nl","local_keywords":["Aruba","One Happy Island","Eagle Beach","Palm Beach","Antilla","Hadicurari","Arikok","Conchi","Oranjestad","flamingo"],"hreflang":["en","nl"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-30"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L1","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Aruba US L1 (lowest tier); south of the hurricane belt (very low storm risk); main concern petty theft; AWG (florin ~1.77/USD), USD accepted almost everywhere"},"si_checklist_25